{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1453553-is-scale-on-weapons-set-by-tags-or-by-narrative-description","id":1453553,"title":"Is scale on weapons set by tags or by narrative description?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-06-26T08:13:12-07:00","id":1453553,"title":"Is scale on weapons set by tags or by narrative description?","content":"My understanding is that basic weapons have a scale of 1. If they have specific tags, they go above that. If they are super science items, they can go above that. The examples for power scaling in Aberrant are a knife at scale 1, a rifle/pistol at scale 2, and an anti-personnel gun at scale 3. I believe this meant to be metaphorical rather than literal. If you throw fireballs at scale 2, your fireballs are about as damaging as being shot with a rifle. Is that correct or should scale actually be used in a more literal interpretation?<br /> <br /> Let's say someone has a knife with maybe a melee and concealable tag. Fair enough, rules as written. Someone brings a pistol to this knife fight. Wouldn't really be Two-Handed, Heavy, let's say this is a run of the mill pistol. It isn't going to be Quality either. We still have the inherit extra oomph that is a pistol. Would this narratively kick it up to scale 2 by the very nature of it being a pistol, or do we hold back and this is in fact a scale 1 item. It will only reach scale 2 with appropriate tags and/or super science.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26906-jeffreybezos","name":"JeffreyBezos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-26T16:51:30-07:00","id":1453610,"title":"","content":"As far as it was discussed here and feed back from devs, regular guns and weapons in general are all scale 1 unless they have tags to that.<br /> <br /> Now, if you want a particularly lethal game, less action movie and more \u201crealistic\u201d, you can give all weapons scale 2, as scale 1 would be your bare hands. A smal knife would be scale 1 too, but a knife, like \u201cthis is a knife\u201d, would be scale 2 too. You could make a -2 tag called bashing or bruising, that makes the weapon scale 1. Honestly, this option takes away a lot of the action feeling, as you can put a character unarmored in critical state with a single shot, but if the idea is to make it lethal, go for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-01T05:29:13-07:00","id":1453921,"title":"","content":"if its aberrrant and then you should give weapons scale.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10020-manifoldpersona","name":"Manifoldpersona","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-01T08:12:18-07:00","id":1453936,"title":"","content":"Honestly, you don\u2019t need to, even in Aberrant.<br /> <br /> You may say novas are powerful and need better adversaries, than let them fight other novas or baselines using Novatech. A regular gun don\u2019t need to be more powerful, actually it need to feel useless against novas, and if you give the gun scale it will make novas feel weaker. It\u2019s much more fun to be Spider-Man if you can dodge bullets from regular criminals, if you need to worrie about every action scene as a possible risk for a super hero or is not that super (heroic yes, not very super)<br /> <br /> An Scale 2 Nova should feel pretty resistant to bullets, and an scale 4 should be completely bullet proof (no even the luckiest lucky can beat this scale gap).<br /> <br /> In the end it will change more the way the players feel about weapons than really the power of the weapons, but yet, and lucky in the dice will have a greater impact on the result of attacks in a higher scale attack, but it\u2019s completely possible both ways in all the games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-01T10:39:25-07:00","id":1453951,"title":"","content":"Honestly, just even bringing durability scale I think is proof enough to how it's meant to be. I completely forgot about that and didn't even take armor into consideration. For sure, any durability scale should allow bullets to drop off. Scale to weapons negates that. Getting around that should in fact be super science. Thanks for the perspective!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26906-jeffreybezos","name":"JeffreyBezos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-09T22:59:46-08:00","id":1467326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1453553-is-scale-on-weapons-set-by-tags-or-by-narrative-description?p=1453610#post1453610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As far as it was discussed here <i><b>and feed back from devs</b></i>, regular guns and weapons in general are all scale 1 unless they have tags to that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could someone please point me to where the devs have said/implied this? Whilst, at my table, we have guns at Scale 2 (as per the table in Core) - I have been looking for a clear statement of intent (if there is one) on the matter because the Combat section &amp; tables of example weapons ignore scale, only referring to the &quot;enhancement&quot; on the weapon. However, going by that, an unarmed strike is the same as a pistol shot which (ignoring the earlier table suggesting guns are Scale 2) seems off to me. A punch being the same power/scale as being shot doesn't feel right at all, even in the &quot;action hero&quot; genre Trinity is striking out for.<br /> <br /> I actually came to the forum today to start a thread talking about this but thought I should search first just to double check if the subject had already been wrong dry. I couldn't find the devs saying this in the &quot;Ask a Dev&quot; thread, despite a couple of posts asking, but happy to read it from ANYWHERE they've said something on the matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26905-eternl-knight","name":"Eternl Knight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26905_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-10T06:16:12-08:00","id":1467347,"title":"","content":"With regards to a pistol vs. a punch, a pistol has an advantage over a punch other than just range, and that is it being a ballistic weapon. In Core Trinity, ballistic armor is harder to come by than impact-resistant armor. Just wearing biking leathers can protect you from a punch, but it's not going to do anything against a pistol.<br /> <br /> One thing to keep in mind when looking at the an example of Scale in the core book is that they were putting out a brand new system. So the examples are not always the best. The system works a lot better if you keep the weapons from the same era the same Scale, barring tags. Scale is not super granular while also being kind of fuzzy. If you want pistols to be more powerful than a punch but not at the Light Anti-tank Weapon level of power, then look at adding and Enhancement to it. That's how more granular differences are handled.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-10T07:52:54-08:00","id":1467357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eternl Knight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1453553-is-scale-on-weapons-set-by-tags-or-by-narrative-description?p=1467326#post1467326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could someone please point me to where the devs have said/implied this? Whilst, at my table, we have guns at Scale 2 (as per the table in Core) - I have been looking for a clear statement of intent (if there is one) on the matter because the Combat section &amp; tables of example weapons ignore scale, only referring to the &quot;enhancement&quot; on the weapon. However, going by that, an unarmed strike is the same as a pistol shot which (ignoring the earlier table suggesting guns are Scale 2) seems off to me. A punch being the same power/scale as being shot doesn't feel right at all, even in the &quot;action hero&quot; genre Trinity is striking out for.<br /> <br /> I actually came to the forum today to start a thread talking about this but thought I should search first just to double check if the subject had already been wrong dry. I couldn't find the devs saying this in the &quot;Ask a Dev&quot; thread, despite a couple of posts asking, but happy to read it from ANYWHERE they've said something on the matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, this discussion happened in 2019 (maybe started in 2018), it\u2019s really hard to find anything in the forums, and at some moment the original Ask the Devs post was deleted and a new one was created.<br /> <br /> As I said before, this game is supposed to be about action movies, where the hero punch can put down a target as well as a shot. The idea when a character is taken out is not about death but not being capable of combat again until get some help, so a punch can knock a person out for long enough for the fight sequence ends.<br /> <br /> You can make it feels different by changing the time it takes to recover from a punch or a shot, a shot will take a few weeks, while a punch a few days (or minutes, in a more action driven game). Each injury may take as long or as little time as need to fit the game, sure a higher level injury will take longer, but a concussion that make you incapable of move your arm and a shattered bone will take different times to heal, even with the same level of injury (both could be maimed).<br /> <br /> Adding scale to a gun shot will make it very lethal, and giving a armor scale to compensate it will turn it into a wall against other attacks. It\u2019s not bad or wrong in any way, it can actually be interesting in a more gritty game, but the general tone of TC would not be the intention.<br /> <br /> Optionally you can reduce the scale of a punch instead, and trained martial artists (anyone with 3 or more dots in Close combat, or anyone with a Martial Art edge, or what ever criteria you prefer) can attack with full scale with their fists. Or give the non-lethal tag to your fists.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s a matter of discuss and set the tone everybody prefer in your table.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-10T18:18:25-08:00","id":1467399,"title":"","content":"OK, without trying to step on toes or rub anyone the wrong way, <i><b>in this thread</b></i> I was only after where I could verify <i><b>the dev's</b></i> intent/opinion. I understand we all have our own views on the matter (and they're all 100% valid at our own tables), but (as I stated above) I was asking here about referenced feedback that I could read for myself . Without casting aspersions at anyone here, when someone says <i>&quot;Person X said this&quot;</i>, I like to verify that they did so rather than rely on second-hand claims about what was &amp; wasn't said. Especially as the books (both Core &amp; Aberrant) both say Pistols are Scale 2, even after errata. \ud83e\udd37<br /> <br /> Thanks to Mateus, I know now that whatever feedback the devs may have given on the subject is now gone (or at least cannot easily be located), so I'll start a thread to discuss our opinions on the matter instead of hijacking this thread (which I responded in only due to the face it was where the feedback was referenced). I'll bring across my responses to the above comments in the new (more focused) thread. Thanks again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26905-eternl-knight","name":"Eternl Knight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26905_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-11T20:26:09-08:00","id":1467518,"title":"","content":"Just to round this thread off with an answer, a dev has (re)stated their intent in another thread which I've copied below.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1467407-the-argument-for-scale-2-firearms?p=1467471#post1467471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The default assumption of the system is that the Scale of guns and armor is appropriate to the Size Scale of the weapon. (Not taking into account any tags.) Humans are Size 1 therefore human-Scale guns and armor are Scale 1. A gun suitable for a car is Scale 2, one for a Jet Fighter Scale 4 etc.<br /> <br /> However, all Scale is relative as defined by the needs of the narrative, and genre emulation comes into this. For action hero genre where the only people who die with one shot are mooks, guns and armor stay at Scale 1 - at most they\u2019ll wound a hero with two Injury Conditions but they won\u2019t kill them. For slightly grittier games, guns and armor can be Scale 2 - getting shot may kill you, and you need armor to defend against it. (If you increase the base Scale of a human-Sized gun, you probably need to increase the Scale of vehicle-mounted guns to match.)<br /> <br /> The key message as applies to TC isn\u2019t \u2018what\u2019s the absolute Scale value does X have\u2019, it\u2019s \u2018what\u2019s the relative difference between X and Y for my game\u2019.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26905-eternl-knight","name":"Eternl Knight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26905_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}